  -> P5b UNDECIDED, and deliberately so. M = 1, 2 and 8 land at 1.0147, 1.0095
     and 0.9977 -- P3 reproduced on a second axis. **M = 4 reads 0.7082 and I
     cannot say why.** Its slice coverage is no worse than M = 8's, so the
     coverage story is wrong; a gate written to exclude it excluded M = 8 instead
     and kept it. Three distinct contamination modes have now appeared at M > 1
     (whole-slice underflow, partial underflow with a spurious peak, and this),
     so the instrument -- reading a ridge off the stationary distribution at
     M > 1 -- is not trustworthy enough to settle the M axis. **Reported as
     unresolved rather than gated until it agrees.** P3 and P4 do not depend on it.

